# ===== Voix -> MIDI — ignore everything that is not a source =====
# Guided results review keeps no persistent state or generated output.

# --- Virtual environments ---
.venv/
venv/
env/
.venv.*/
ENV/

# --- Python cache ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.cache/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# --- Build / distribution ---
build/
dist/
wheels/
*.whl
pip-wheel-metadata/

# --- Coverage & quality tools ---
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
.tox/
.nox/
coverage.xml

# --- Machine-local dot-folders at the root ---
# The project's own dot-folder (.github/) is whitelisted just below; any other
# dot-file or dot-folder at the root is local data, never a source to version.
/.*
!/.github/
!/.gitignore
!/.gitattributes

# --- Vendored third-party folder ---
# ONE third-party folder is vendored on purpose, so every clone reviews the
# same instructions: it travels with its MIT license, and `vendor-lock.json`
# pins the upstream commit it was copied from (see AGENTS.md). Everything
# else under vendor/ stays machine-local; the project's own rules live in
# AGENTS.md.
/vendor/*
!/vendor/make-interfaces-feel-better/
!/vendor/make-interfaces-feel-better/**
!/vendor/make-interfaces-feel-better-LICENSE

# --- Generated audio artifacts (analysis, demo, tests) ---
# Live take folders include immutable automatic/corrected reading archives.
*.wav
*.mp3
*.flac
*.ogg
*.m4a
*.aac
*.mid
*.midi
/live_*
prises_live/
# persisted vocal observations (analysis and replay share <take>.observation.npz)
*.npz

# --- Analysis outputs: scores + reports (export_result) ---
# Everything the pipeline writes with an arbitrary prefix:
# .musicxml / .pdf (MuseScore-LilyPond engraving) / .json / .csv
# Coherence, intonation registers, closed labels and live/final rates share these outputs.
*.musicxml
*.pdf
*.json
*.csv
# NB: the repo tracks no .json/.csv/.pdf today; should a JSON config file
# ever be tracked, negotiate it here with a !.

# exceptions: keep a possibly versioned sample audio, and the test
# artifacts reference (tests/reference/artifacts.json, see AGENTS.md):
# it is a fingerprint, not an analysis output — it must be tracked.
!tests/data/*.wav
!tests/reference/*.json
# the vendored folder's lockfile (see AGENTS.md): an upstream pin, not an
# analysis output — and it must come AFTER the `*.json` rule to win
!/vendor-lock.json
# the web page's own sources: its two-language labels and the frozen answers
# the JavaScript port replays (web/, see AGENTS.md) — the segmentation cases,
# the two YIN readings, and the intonation summary the visible line prints
!/web/strings.json
!/web/test/cases.json
!/web/test/yin.json
!/web/test/yin-rates.json
!/web/test/intonation.json
# NB: demo.wav stays ignored (make_demo.py regenerates it), so yin.json and
# yin-rates.json are the committed half of those comparisons and must NEVER be
# ignored.

# --- IDE / editors ---
.idea/
.vscode/
*.sublime-project
*.sublime-workspace
*.swp
*.swo

# --- OS ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# --- Docker (local files, exported images) ---
*.tar
docker-compose.override.yml

# --- Personal notes ---
*.log

# --- Local runs (throwable root validation files) ---
/demo_out.*
/test68.*
/demo_docker.*
/demo_t1.*
/demo_t2.*
/demo_dbg.*
/_ours.pdf
/_via_py.pdf
# temporary captures and logs of the GUI / PDF checks (including home-screen layout)
/shot_*.png
# the Pages workflow's 1600 px screenshot (web/test/wide-shot.mjs)
/wide-*.png
# the home page's before/after captures: evidence for a UI review, not sources
/page-prise-*.png
# Root docs: only the NAMED files are sources. AGENTS.md (project rules),
# CONTEXT.md (domain glossary), SKILLS.md (procedures), the two READMEs and
# constraints.txt travel with a clone; any other root .md/.txt — audit,
# diagnostic or proposal reports, the throwaway notes about the problems
# being worked on — stays local, and their conclusions live in AGENTS.md,
# CONTEXT.md and the ADRs.
/*.md
/*.txt
!/AGENTS.md
!/CONTEXT.md
!/SKILLS.md
!/README.md
!/README.fr.md
!/constraints.txt
/_dbg.log
/out_dir
adr/
# Design notes that travel with the code: the docs under docs/project/ and
# the hardware recipe are part of the project. The ADRs, dated reports, captures,
# docs/engine-drift.md and docs/superpowers/ stay local and are ignored.
/docs/*
!/docs/project/
!/docs/project/**
!/docs/recette-materielle-navigateurs.md
/out*
# prises_verite: the TAKES and truths stay personal (wav/json), but the
# README committing the format and the non-drift fingerprints are tracked
/prises_verite/*
!/prises_verite/README.md
!/prises_verite/*.fingerprint.json
.superpowers
# the web matrix job borrows Playwright at test time; the page stays dependency-free
/node_modules/
